<section id="about" class="relative px-5 md:px-10 py-24 md:py-36">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-marker mb-4">The Story</p>
    <h2 class="font-[var(--font-display)] uppercase font-black leading-[0.85] text-[clamp(2.5rem,8vw,6rem)] ink-stamp mb-12">
      A One-Day Press<br />on Abbot Kinney
    </h2>

    <div class="prose-lg text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed space-y-6 max-w-none opacity-95">
      <p>
        Blockprint is a one-day block party in the heart of Venice — a single
        afternoon where we shut down a stretch of Abbot Kinney and turn it into
        a festival on the street itself. Electronic music, local food, art, and
        Venice culture, all on one block.
      </p>
      <p>
        We close 3–4 blocks of Abbot Kinney Blvd between Brooks and San Juan,
        run a single stage end-to-end, and pull in the artists, restaurants,
        and shops that make this stretch of the city what it is. No second
        stage, no shuttle from a parking lot, no fenced-off VIP island —
        just one street, one afternoon, one crowd.
      </p>
      <p>
        The name comes from the craft: a single sheet, pressed once, never
        quite the same as the last one. That's the festival we want to throw —
        singular, unpolished in the right places, and built for the people
        standing in the room.
      </p>
      <p class="text-bp-pink font-semibold">
        August 22, 2026 · 3–9 PM · Abbot Kinney Blvd · 21 and over.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
